// lineage.config — turn on Nextflow's native data lineage (25.04+).
//
// Why this is separate from petri.config:
//   petri.config sets maxForks = 1 to make the QUEUED state visible on the
//   dashboard. That serialises the run, which is fine for a 1-donor demo and
//   painful for 5. Lineage has nothing to do with that trade, so it lives here
//   and the two can be combined or used independently.
//
// What it does:
//   Records every run, task, output file and the links between them into a
//   lineage store, addressable by lid:// URIs. Query it with:
//
//       nextflow lineage list
//
//   Lineage is NOT retroactive. Only runs launched with this enabled are
//   recorded; existing runs in work/ have none.
//
// Note: `store.location` may not be the exact key for your Nextflow version -
// check `nextflow.io/docs/latest/data-lineage.html` before relying on it. The
// `enabled` flag is the part that matters.

lineage {
    enabled = true
}
